; setquad_sample_register: the quadratic opcodes require MODEL mode.
;
; A sample carries no quadratic storage, so SETQUAD on one has nowhere to
; write. Accepting the write would grow a `quadratic` map the sample's own
; accessors never read back, and GETQUAD would return 0 (QUI-1160).
;
; The fault is TYPE_MISMATCH (RegisterType).
;
; The indices are in range and the value is ordinary, so nothing but the
; register's mode is at fault.

PUSH 4
BSMX r0          ; a SAMPLE, not a model

PUSH 0           ; i
PUSH 1           ; j
PUSH 5           ; value
SETQUAD r0
HALT
